gOg(){return"A sign warning of a crossing with a barrier?"},
gOf(){return"Yes. Ahead is a railway crossing with a barrier."},
gOi(){return"Is it possible to overtake 80 meters before the crossing?"},
gOh(){return"No. Overtaking is prohibited at a crossing and 100 m before it (clause 11.4)."},
gOk(){return"Can I park my car 30 meters from the crossing?"},
gOj(){return"No. Parking is prohibited closer than 50 m from the crossing (clause 12.5)."},
gOu(){return"Is there a crossing ahead without a barrier?"},
gOt(){return"Yes. The sign warns about crossing without a barrier."},
gOw(){return"Can I turn around at the crossing?"},
gOv(){return"No. At the crossing, turning and reversing are prohibited (clauses 8.11\u20138.12)."},
gOy(){return"Is there only one railway track at the crossing?"},
gOx(){return"Yes. This sign indicates a crossing with one path, without a barrier."},
gOA(){return"Is this sign placed 150\u2013300 m before the crossing?"},
gOz(){return"No. Sign 1.3.1 is placed immediately before the crossing."},
gOC(){return"The tram crosses the road outside the intersection, not from the depot. Should I give way?"},
gOB(){return"Yes. Outside the intersection, the tram has priority except for leaving the depot (clause 18.1)."},
gOE(){return"The tram leaves the depot. Should it give way to cars?"},
gOD(){return"Yes. When leaving the depot, the tram gives way to other vehicles (clause 18.1)."},
gOG(){return"Without a traffic light at an equivalent intersection, do you need to give way to the car on the right?"},
gOF(){return"Yes. At an uncontrolled intersection of equal significance, give way to cars on the right (clause 13.11)."},
gOI(){return"Is it possible to overtake at an equivalent intersection without a traffic light?"},
gOH(){return"No. At an uncontrolled intersection, overtaking is allowed only when driving on the main road (clause 11.4)."},
gOK(){return"Is there a roundabout ahead?"},
gOJ(){return"Yes. A sign warns you when approaching a roundabout."},
gOM(){return"Does the roundabout start right at this sign?"},
gOL(){return"No. This is a warning. The direction of movement on the circle itself is set by sign 4.3."},
gOc(){return"Is it possible to turn around if the road is only visible at 70 m?"},
gOb(){return"No. To turn around, visibility must be at least 100 m in each direction (clause 8.11)."},
gOe(){return"Before a dangerous turn, should you choose a safe speed?"},
gOd(){return"Yes. The speed is chosen taking into account the turn and visibility of the road (clause 10.1)."},
gOm(){return"Could children suddenly come onto the road here?"},
gOl(){return"Yes. The sign warns of an area where children may appear on the road."},
gOo(){return"Does this sign allow children to cross the road anywhere?"},
gOn(){return"No. The sign warns drivers, but does not change the rules for crossing the road."},
gOq(){return"A temporary sign on a yellow background is more important than a permanent one if they conflict?"},
gOp(){return"Yes. If there is a contradiction between temporary and permanent signs, the temporary requirement is fulfilled."},
gOs(){return"Do you have to stop at a road works sign?"},
gOr(){return"No. The sign itself does not require stopping. You need to take roadworks into account and choose a safe speed."},
gOO(){return"Without a traffic light, do you have the right of way over a car with a second priority?"},
gON(){return"Yes. At an uncontrolled intersection, the main road gives priority over the secondary one (clause 13.9)."},
gOQ(){return"Is it possible to drive on a red light if you are on the main road?"},
gOP(){return"No. At a signalized intersection, you must follow the traffic lights (clause 6.15)."},
gOS(){return"Is it possible to park a car on the roadway of a main road outside a populated area?"},
gOR(){return"No. On such roads, parking on the roadway outside a populated area is prohibited (clause 12.5)."},
gOU(){return"Does the sign mark the end of the main road?"},
gOT(){return"Yes. The advantage that the \u201cMain Road\u201d sign gave is ending."},
gOW(){return"Does this sign itself require you to stop?"},
gOV(){return"No. It revokes the main road status. The order of travel is determined by other signs and rules."},
gOY(){return"Without a traffic light, should a car from the road you are crossing have to give way to you?"},
gOX(){return"Yes. The sign shows the intersection of the main road with the secondary one (clause 13.9)."},
gP_(){return"Without a traffic light, do you need to give way to a car on the right from a secondary road?"},
gOZ(){return"No. You have the advantage: you are on the main road. The \u201cinterference from the right\u201d rule does not apply here."},
gP1(){return"Without a traffic light, do you need to give way to cars on the road you are crossing?"},
gP0(){return"Yes. The sign requires you to give way to cars on the road you are crossing. With plate 8.13, you give way to cars on the main road."},
gP3(){return"The road is clear. Do you still need to stop at this sign?"},
gP2(){return"No. There is no mandatory stop if you are not disturbing anyone."},
gP5(){return"Both are on the secondary road: you are going straight, and the oncoming car is turning left. Should he give way?"},
gP4(){return"Yes. With equal priority, an oncoming car turning left gives way to the one going straight (clause 13.12)."},
gP7(){return"Do you need to stop before STOP, even if the road is clear?"},
gP6(){return"Yes. Stop in front of the stop line, and if there is none, in front of the edge of the roadway you are crossing. At a crossing without a stop line - in front of the sign."},
gP9(){return"Is it possible to drive STOP without stopping if everything is clearly visible?"},
gP8(){return"No. The sign requires a complete stop even when the road is clear."},
gPb(){return"The entry will interfere with the oncoming car. Should I give way?"},
gPa(){return"Yes. You must not drive into a narrow area if it will impede oncoming traffic."},
gPd(){return"Does this sign give you an advantage over oncoming vehicles?"},
gPc(){return"No. Oncoming traffic has the right of way."},
gPf(){return"Do you have an advantage in a narrow area?"},
gPe(){return"Yes. This sign gives you an advantage over oncoming cars."},
gPh(){return"Does this sign give an oncoming car the right of way?"},
gPg(){return"No. Transport moving in your direction has priority."},
gPv(){return"Is this sign prohibiting entry for regular taxis?"},
gPu(){return"Yes. Taxis and car sharing must comply with the ban. The exception is route transport."},
gPx(){return"Can you move in just because you live behind the sign?"},
gPw(){return"No. There is no exception for residents. Do not confuse this sign with sign 3.2 \u201cMovement Prohibition\u201d."},
gPz(){return"Can a shuttle bus enter on its route?"},
gPy(){return"Yes. The prohibition of this sign does not apply to route vehicles."},
